# Day 01 — Linux Basics

Linux is a free and open-source operating system based on Unix kernel.
Created by Linus Torvalds in 1991.
It is more stable and secure system.It is listed under GNU General Public License.

###About Shell
Several kinds of SHELL.
1. sh - Bourne shell is the oldest(1970).
2. bash - Bourne-Again Shell is default shell for most linux.
3. zsh- Z shell improve vershion of bash.
4. shh - like sh(Bourne shell but more earlier version).
5. ksh - Korn shell
6. csh - C shell
7. tcsh - improve version of csh shell.

### What command I learn.
1. echo $SHELL - return default or preferred shell.
2. echo $0 - return to current shell. 
3. ls - list the directory and files in current user
4. ls -l - long formated list with permission of file list
5. ls -a - list all hidden files
6 ls -lh - list in human readable form 
7. pwd - print working directory
8. clear - clear the terminal
9. history - keeps history of all run command
10. cd <directory>- change directory
11. cd .. - go bak to directory.
12. man <command> - gives the information about the command
13. info <command> - gives the information of the command.
14. alias ld='ls -a' - create the short form of ls -a
15. /etc/bashrc - location of default alias
16. ~/.bashrc - user created alias

